<style>[data-pf-type=Paragraph3] a{color:#ce181e!important;text-decoration:none!important}[data-pf-type=Paragraph3] a:hover{text-decoration:underline!important}</style><div data-pf-editor-version="legacy" class="sc-fUBjpT fIEUnj __pf __pf_42FASkbj" id="__pf"><div data-pf-type="Body" class="sc-boZfnm jvQCDP pf-9_"><div data-pf-type="Layout" class="sc-hGMjVM jaEIjy pf-10_"><div data-section-id="pf-6df0" data-category="Page Introduction" data-name="Cottage" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-fscnvs bBcbzk pf-11_ pf-color-scheme-1 pf-bg-lazy"><div style="--cw:1400px" class="sc-iowYbt LsuWb"><div class="sc-ibQzxG cSbAnC pf-12_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-13_ pf-bg-lazy"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0691/3340/2417/t/25/assets/5-step-lawn-logo-white_web-1683571057282_331x.png?v=1683571058" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0691/3340/2417/t/25/assets/5-step-lawn-logo-white_web-1683571057282.png?v=1683571058 1536w" width="331" height="215" sizes="(min-width: 1536px) 1536px, (min-width: 1024px) 1280px, (min-width: 640px) 768px, calc(100vw/3)" loading="lazy" alt="5 Step Lawn Program" title="5 Step Lawn Program" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-kUdmUV QtCYW pf-14_ pf-image-1 h1"/><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-15_ pf-heading-6-h3">Each round provides a step-by-step guide to keeping lawns healthy all year.&nbsp;</h3><div data-pf-type="Tabs" class="sc-iA-DtKN iHtWiw pf-17_"><div data-pf-type="TabsMenu" class="sc-fEiJeM qQLOw pf-18_"><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="false" class="sc-kBRnVi bnhtCk pf-19_ pf-anchor" contenteditable="false" data-pf-type="TabHeader2">Round 1</button><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="false" class="sc-kBRnVi bnhtCk pf-21_ pf-anchor" contenteditable="false" data-pf-type="TabHeader2">Round 2</button><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="false" class="sc-kBRnVi bnhtCk pf-23_ pf-anchor" contenteditable="false" data-pf-type="TabHeader2">Round 3</button><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="false" class="sc-kBRnVi bnhtCk pf-25_ pf-anchor" contenteditable="false" data-pf-type="TabHeader2">Round 4</button><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="true" class="sc-kBRnVi bnhtCk pf-27_ pf-anchor" contenteditable="false" data-pf-type="TabHeader2">Round 5</button></div><div data-pf-type="TabContentWrapper" class="sc-ciQpcn iMJEsI pf-29_"><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:none" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-iZzLKd hZePKj pf-30_"><div class="sc-ibQzxG cSbAnC pf-31_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:8;--c-md:8;--c-lg:8"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-32_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-33_ pf-heading-6-h3">EARLY SPRING</h3><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-35_ pf-heading-3-h3">Pre-Emergent Crabgrass Prevention</h3><p class="sc-fbFjKN fqkBeE pf-37_ pf-text-2" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Applying a granular <a href="/collections/fertilizers" target="_self">fertilizer</a> in early spring helps&nbsp;promote strong green-up and supports recovery from winter stress. For best results, choose a&nbsp;<a href="/collections/pre-emergent-fertilizers" target="_self">fertilizer with a pre-emergent</a> <a href="https://collections/pre-emergent-fertilizers" target="_self">herbicide</a>, which helps prevent annual summer weeds such as crabgrass.<br><br><b>Timing is Critical<br></b>The effectiveness of pre-emergent herbicides is highly dependent on weather and proper timing.<br><br><strong>•	Avoid applying too early</strong>—the product must remain active for approximately 14–16 weeks (varies by rainfall and product).<br>
<br><strong>•</strong>	In the Upper Midwest, <strong>crabgrass germination generally occurs around June 1</strong>, though this can shift with seasonal weather patterns.<br><br><strong>Important Notes:<br>• </strong>Pre-emergent fertilizers do not prevent spring dandelions.<br><strong>•</strong> Applying weed &amp; feed early will not stop spring dandelions.<br><strong>•</strong> These products target annual grassy weeds, not broadleaf weeds that emerege earlier in the season.<br><br>Read more about&nbsp;<strong><a href="/blogs/powering-productivity/crabgrass-prevention-and-timing" target="_self">Crabgrass Prevention and Timing</a></strong></p><a href="/collections/pre-emergent-fertilizers" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-39_ pf-button-2">Shop Pre-Emergents</a><a href="/collections/turf-spreaders" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-41_ pf-button-2">Shop Fertilizer&nbsp;Spreaders</a></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-43_"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0691/3340/2417/t/25/assets/5steplawnprogramround1-1684933114026.webp?v=1684933122" loading="lazy" width="300" height="300" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-kUdmUV QtCYW pf-44_ pf-image-1"/></div></div></div></div><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:none" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-iZzLKd hZePKj pf-45_"><div class="sc-ibQzxG cSbAnC pf-46_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:8;--c-md:8;--c-lg:8"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-47_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-48_ pf-heading-6-h3">LATE SPRING / EARLY SUMMER</h3><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-50_ pf-heading-3-h3">Late Spring Feeding or Weed &amp; Feed</h3><p class="sc-fbFjKN fqkBeE pf-52_ pf-text-2" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">As temperatures warm and lawns become more active, applying a granular fertilizer—either a&nbsp;<a href="/collections/straight-fertlizers" target="_self">straight fertilizer</a> or <a href="/collections/weed-feed-fertilizers" target="_self">weed &amp; feed</a>&nbsp;product—provides essential nutrients to <strong>enhance lawn color, thickness, and overall vigor</strong>. <br><br>Products containing time released nitrogen deliver steady feeding over several weeks, promoting sustained growth without excessive surge.<br><br><strong>Broadleaf Weed Control<br></strong>During late spring, broadleaf weeds such as dandelions are actively growing and respond well to treatment. <br><br>To keep your lawn looking its best, we recommend a blanket application of a liquid or granular broadleaf herbicide, or the use of a <a href="/collections/weed-feed-fertilizers" target="_self">weed &amp; feed</a>&nbsp;product. This helps significantly reduce visible weeds and improves overall lawn appearance heading into summer.<br><br>Click the link below to learn more!
<br><a href="/blogs/powering-productivity/the-ultimate-guide-to-weed-feed-timing-techniques-and-tips" target="_self"><strong><span style="color: rgb(208, 2, 27);">The Ultimate Guide to Weed &amp; Feed: Timing, Techniques, and Tips</span></strong></a></p><a href="/collections/straight-fertlizers" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-54_ pf-button-2">Shop Straight&nbsp;Fertilizer</a><a href="/collections/weed-feed-fertilizers" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-56_ pf-button-2">Shop Weed &amp; Feed&nbsp;Fertilizer</a><a href="/collections/turf-herbicides" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-58_ pf-button-2">Shop Herbicides</a></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-60_"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0691/3340/2417/t/25/assets/5steplawnprogramround2-1684933114024.webp?v=1684933120" loading="lazy" width="300" height="300" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-kUdmUV QtCYW pf-61_ pf-image-1"/></div></div></div></div><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:none" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-iZzLKd hZePKj pf-62_"><div class="sc-ibQzxG cSbAnC pf-63_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:8;--c-md:8;--c-lg:8"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-64_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-65_ pf-heading-6-h3">SUMMER</h3><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-67_ pf-heading-3-h3">Summer Fertilizer &amp; Grub Prevention</h3><p class="sc-fbFjKN fqkBeE pf-69_ pf-text-2" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Keeping a lawn healthy through the heat of summer can be challenging. While most lawns look great in April and May, maintaining that color and density during hot, dry weather requires proper nutrition and preventative pest control.<br><br><strong>Fertilizer + Grub Prevention (Recommended)</strong><br>A slow release granular fertilizer combined with a&nbsp;<a href="/collections/insecticide-fertilizers" target="_self">preventative systemic insecticide</a> is the best way to support summer growth and prevent damage from grubs before they appear.&nbsp;For the best results, apply these products between <strong>June 15 and August 1</strong>.<br><br><strong>This application provides:<br>•	</strong>Sustained feeding during summer stress.<br><strong>•</strong>	Protection against white grubs before they hatch.<br><strong>•	</strong>Improved color, thickness, and root strength.
<br><br><strong>If You Choose NOT to Apply a Grub Preventer<br></strong>Straight summer fertilization is still highly recommended. Strong nutrition helps the lawn maintain color and vigor through heat and drought.<br><br>✔ Mid-Range nitrogen — Polymer coated to reduce the risk of lawn burn
<br>✔ Iron added to boosts deep green color
<br>✔ Safe, slow release nutrition ideal for summer conditions<br><br><a href="/blogs/powering-productivity/grub-control-how-to-evict-lawn-pests-before-they-move-in" target="_self"><strong>Learn more about Grub Control &amp; Grub Preventative</strong></a><br>
</p><a href="/collections/insecticide-fertilizers" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-71_ pf-button-2">Shop Insecticide Fertilizers</a><a href="/collections/summer-fertilizer" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-73_ pf-button-2">Shop Summer Fertilizers</a><a href="/collections/crabgrass-control-products" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-75_ pf-button-2">Shop Crabgrass Control</a><a href="/collections/watering-supplies" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-77_ pf-button-2">Shop Watering Supplies</a><a href="/collections/insecticides" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-79_ pf-button-2">Shop Insecticides</a><a href="/collections/turf-herbicides" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-81_ pf-button-2">Shop Herbicides</a></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-83_"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0691/3340/2417/t/25/assets/5steplawnprogramround3-1684933114018.webp?v=1684933118" loading="lazy" width="300" height="300" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-kUdmUV QtCYW pf-84_ pf-image-1"/></div></div></div></div><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:none" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-iZzLKd hZePKj pf-85_"><div class="sc-ibQzxG cSbAnC pf-86_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:8;--c-md:8;--c-lg:8"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-87_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-88_ pf-heading-6-h3">LATE SUMMER / EARLY FALL</h3><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-90_ pf-heading-3-h3">Late Summer Feeding or Weed &amp; Feed</h3><p class="sc-fbFjKN fqkBeE pf-92_ pf-text-2" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Late summer is an important time to strengthen your lawn as it recovers from heat stress and prepares for fall growth. Applying a granular fertilizer (<a href="/collections/fertilizers" target="_self">straight fertilizer</a> or <a href="/collections/weed-feed-fertilizers" target="_self">weed &amp; feed fertilizer</a>) that contains&nbsp;time-released nitrogen helps&nbsp;promote deeper root development and repair damage from summer conditions.<br><br><strong>Broadleaf Weed Control<br></strong>We recommend a second blanket application of a liquid or granular broadleaf herbicide (or a weed &amp; feed product) during this period. This treatment helps manage broadleaf weeds such as dandelions, which often rebound later in the season.<br><br><strong>Grub Worm Treatment<br></strong>The second half of summer is when grub worms begin to emerge, typically resulting from beetle eggs laid in June and July. Once grubs are present and feeding, quick action is needed.
<br><br>For fast and effective curative control, we recommend:&nbsp;<a href="/products/the-andersons-duocide-curative-insecticide-40lb-aptdgdu4" target="_self">Duocide </a>or <a href="/products/dylox-6-2-granular-insecticide-30-lb-bag" target="_self">Dylox</a>. These products are designed for active grub infestations and work quickly to minimize lawn damage.
<br><br><strong>Aeration</strong><br>Late summer into early fall is also an ideal time for core aeration which is an important part of maintaining a healthy, resilient lawn.<br><br><strong>Aerating the lawn helps:
<br></strong>•	Reduce soil compaction
<br>•	Improve oxygen flow
<br>•	Enhance nutrient and water absorption
<br>•	Support stronger root growth heading into fall<br></p><a href="/collections/weed-feed-fertilizers" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-94_ pf-button-2">Shop Weed &amp; Feed Fertilizers</a><a href="/blogs/powering-productivity/fall-lawn-care-basics" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-96_ pf-button-2">Fall Lawn Basics - Learn More</a><a href="/collections/insecticides" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-98_ pf-button-2">Shop Insecticides</a><a href="/collections/aerators" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button2" class="sc-kgvFNj cPdmrl pf-100_ pf-button-2">Shop Aerators</a></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-102_"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0691/3340/2417/t/25/assets/5steplawnprogramround4-1684933114016.webp?v=1684933116" loading="lazy" width="300" height="300" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-kUdmUV QtCYW pf-103_ pf-image-1"/></div></div></div></div><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:block" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-iZzLKd hZePKj pf-104_"><div class="sc-ibQzxG cSbAnC pf-105_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:8;--c-md:8;--c-lg:8"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-jwZJYP cIFzrt pf-106_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-107_ pf-heading-6-h3">LATE FALL</h3><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-bOhtQk gAzRSI pf-109_ pf-heading-3-h3">Winterizer</h3><p class="sc-fbFjKN fqkBeE pf-111_ pf-text-2" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">The final—and most important—lawn care application of the year is the winterizer treatment. Applying a granular fertilizer with high nitrogen content and low, slow release nitrogen helps prepare your lawn for harsh winter conditions.
<br><br><strong>This application provides:
<br></strong>•	Improved winter hardiness
<br>•	Greater durability during temperature fluctuations
<br>•	Enhanced root strength for winter survival
<br>•	A faster, healthier spring green up
<br><br>A properly timed winterizer feeding ensures your lawn stores the nutrients it needs to thrive when growth resumes in early spring.
